#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Migrate from using the IBM Quantum cloud simulators to using Qiskit Runtime "
"local testing mode."
msgstr ""
"Mag-migrate mula sa paggamit ng IBM Quantum cloud simulators patungo sa "
"Qiskit Runtime local testing mode."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate to local simulators"
msgstr "Mag-migrate sa mga lokal na simulator"

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate to local simulators {#migrate-to-local-simulators}"
msgstr "Mag-migrate sa mga lokal na simulator {#migrate-to-local-simulators}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In quantum computing, the choice between using simulators and quantum "
"hardware is crucial for making progress in the field. While simulators are "
"useful for testing and debugging, in this era of quantum utility, quantum "
"development and industry advancement requires actual hardware. As part of "
"the move to quantum utility, IBM Quantum&reg; cloud simulators were retired "
"on 15 May 2024. This guide explains the retirement in more detail, and how "
"to migrate from cloud-based simulators, such as `ibmq_qasm_simulator`, to "
"local simulators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa quantum computing, ang pagpili sa pagitan ng paggamit ng mga simulator at"
" quantum hardware ay mahalaga para makapag-unlad sa larangan. Bagama't "
"kapaki-pakinabang ang mga simulator para sa pag-test at pag-debug, sa "
"panahon ng quantum utility, ang pag-unlad ng quantum at pag-asenso ng "
"industriya ay nangangailangan ng tunay na hardware. Bilang bahagi ng "
"paglipat sa quantum utility, ang IBM Quantum&reg; cloud simulators ay na-"
"retire noong 15 Mayo 2024. Ipinapaliwanag ng gabay na ito ang retirement "
"nang mas detalyado, at kung paano mag-migrate mula sa mga cloud-based na "
"simulator, tulad ng `ibmq_qasm_simulator`, patungo sa mga lokal na "
"simulator.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Why are the cloud simulators being retired? {#why-are-the-cloud-simulators-"
"being-retired}"
msgstr ""
"Bakit ino-retire ang mga cloud simulator? {#why-are-the-cloud-simulators-"
"being-retired}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The cloud simulators are being retired for several reasons:\n"
msgstr "Ino-retire ang mga cloud simulator dahil sa ilang dahilan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Simulators have limitations\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"May mga limitasyon ang mga simulator\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Simulators can be useful, but they are too limited to use for research or "
"experimentation:\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaaring maging kapaki-pakinabang ang mga simulator, ngunit masyadong "
"limitado ang mga ito para gamitin sa pananaliksik o eksperimentasyon:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Simulators are valuable for understanding small-scale QPUs (quantum "
"processing units), but their usefulness maxes out at around 50 qubits, even "
"with access to high-performance supercomputers. This ceiling comes from the "
"exponential growth in computational resources required to simulate larger "
"quantum computers (review [Massively parallel quantum computer simulator, "
"eleven years later](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.04708) for the full "
"explanation).  Exploring quantum computers of 100 qubits and more requires "
"hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mahalaga ang mga simulator para maunawaan ang maliliit na QPU (quantum "
"processing units), ngunit hanggang sa humigit-kumulang 50 qubit lang ang "
"kanilang pagiging kapaki-pakinabang, kahit may access sa mga high-"
"performance na supercomputer. Nagmumula ang ceiling na ito sa exponential na"
" paglago ng kinakailangang computational resources para i-simulate ang mas "
"malalaking quantum computer (basahin ang [Massively parallel quantum "
"computer simulator, eleven years later](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.04708) "
"para sa buong paliwanag). Ang pag-explore ng mga quantum computer na may 100"
" qubit pataas ay nangangailangan ng hardware.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While some simulators offer noise models, it is a very hard problem to "
"capture the entire dynamics of a real QPU. Quantum hardware offers the "
"potential for researchers to confront the challenges inherent in quantum "
"computers, such as noise, errors, and decoherence in a realistic testing "
"environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagama't nag-aalok ang ilang simulator ng mga noise model, napakahirap na "
"capture ang buong dynamics ng isang tunay na QPU. Nag-aalok ang quantum "
"hardware ng potensyal para harapin ng mga mananaliksik ang mga hamon na "
"likas sa mga quantum computer, tulad ng noise, errors, at decoherence sa "
"isang makatotohanang testing environment.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "</AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr "</AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<AccordionItem title=\"Using quantum hardware builds unique skills\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Nagpapaunlad ng natatanging kasanayan ang paggamit ng"
" quantum hardware\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Interacting with quantum hardware grows skills and experience unattainable "
"by only using simulators:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pakikipag-ugnayan sa quantum hardware ay nagpapaunlad ng mga kasanayan "
"at karanasang hindi makukuha sa pamamagitan lamang ng paggamit ng mga "
"simulator:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Direct interaction with quantum hardware builds skills because you must "
"implement or use error mitigation or suppression techniques, for reliable "
"computation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang direktang pakikipag-ugnayan sa quantum hardware ay nagpapatibay ng mga "
"kasanayan dahil kailangang mag-implement o gumamit ng mga error mitigation o"
" suppression na teknik para sa maaasahang computation.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Hands-on experience with quantum hardware develops a deeper understanding of"
" quantum phenomena and how to tailor algorithms to the characteristics of "
"quantum processors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang hands-on na karanasan sa quantum hardware ay nagpapaunlad ng mas malalim"
" na pag-unawa sa mga quantum phenomena at kung paano i-tailor ang mga "
"algorithm sa mga katangian ng mga quantum processor.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Engaging with quantum hardware results in practical insights into the "
"challenges and opportunities of quantum computing, enhancing developers' "
"ability to drive innovation in the field.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pakikipag-ugnayan sa quantum hardware ay nagbubunga ng mga praktikal na "
"insight sa mga hamon at oportunidad ng quantum computing, na nagpapalakas ng"
" kakayahan ng mga developer na mag-drive ng inobasyon sa larangan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Algorithms should be adapted for quantum "
"hardware\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Dapat i-adapt ang mga algorithm para sa quantum "
"hardware\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Successful quantum algorithms must be adapted to exploit the capabilities of"
" quantum hardware, optimizing performance and efficiency.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga matagumpay na quantum algorithm ay dapat i-adapt para samantalahin "
"ang mga kakayahan ng quantum hardware, na nino-optimize ang performance at "
"efficiency.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum hardware provides a more accurate representation of real-world QPUs "
"than simulators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagbibigay ang quantum hardware ng mas tumpak na representasyon ng mga tunay"
" na QPU kaysa sa mga simulator.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fine-tuning algorithms for quantum hardware involves adjusting ansatz, "
"circuit implementations, parameters, and configuration to maximize "
"performance.  This process is best achieved through direct experimentation "
"with quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang fine-tuning ng mga algorithm para sa quantum hardware ay kinabibilangan "
"ng pag-aayos ng ansatz, circuit implementations, parameters, at "
"configuration para ma-maximize ang performance. Pinakamainam na makamit ang "
"prosesong ito sa pamamagitan ng direktang eksperimentasyon sa quantum "
"hardware.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "When should simulators be used? {#when-should-simulators-be-used}"
msgstr ""
"Kailan dapat gamitin ang mga simulator? {#when-should-simulators-be-used}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum simulators should be used to help develop and test programs before "
"fine-tuning them and sending them to quantum hardware. Local simulators can "
"do this with good performance and efficiency.  Clifford circuits can be "
"simulated very efficiently, and results can be verified, which is a useful "
"way to gain confidence in an experiment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga quantum simulator ay dapat gamitin para tulungang mag-develop at "
"mag-test ng mga programa bago i-fine-tune ang mga ito at ipadala sa quantum "
"hardware. Magagawa ng mga lokal na simulator ang ganitong trabaho nang may "
"magandang performance at efficiency. Ang mga Clifford circuit ay maaaring "
"i-simulate nang napaka-episyente, at maaaring ma-verify ang mga resulta, na "
"isang kapaki-pakinabang na paraan para makakuha ng kumpiyansa sa isang "
"eksperimento.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Local testing mode does not have built-in error suppression or mitigation.  Instead, you must specify those options explicitly. See [Configure error mitigation for Qiskit Runtime](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques) for details.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Ang local testing mode ay walang built-in na error suppression o mitigation. Sa halip, kailangan mong tukuyin nang malinaw ang mga opsyong iyon. Tingnan ang [I-configure ang error mitigation para sa Qiskit Runtime](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques) para sa mga detalye.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate to local simulators {#migrate-to-local-simulators-1}"
msgstr ""
"Mag-migrate sa mga lokal na simulator {#migrate-to-local-simulators-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With `qiskit-ibm-runtime` 0.22.0 or later, you can use local testing mode to"
" replace cloud simulators. Depending on your needs, there are several ways "
"to use local testing mode.  To begin, specify one of the fake backends in "
"``qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider`` or specify a Qiskit Aer backend when "
"instantiating a primitive or a session.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa `qiskit-ibm-runtime` 0.22.0 o mas bago, maaari kang gumamit ng local "
"testing mode para palitan ang mga cloud simulator. Depende sa iyong mga "
"pangangailangan, may ilang paraan para gamitin ang local testing mode. Para "
"magsimula, tumukoy ng isa sa mga fake backend sa "
"``qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider`` o tumukoy ng Qiskit Aer backend kapag "
"nag-instantiate ng primitive o session.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Guidance for choosing a simulator {#guidance-for-choosing-a-simulator}"
msgstr "Gabay sa pagpili ng simulator {#guidance-for-choosing-a-simulator}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Use the following table to help choose a simulator.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamitin ang sumusunod na talahanayan para tulungang pumili ng simulator.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Simulator           | Fake Backends                                   | AerSimulator                                       | Clifford Simulation                                |\n"
"|---------------------|-------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|\n"
"| **Purpose**         | Mimics specific IBM&reg; QPUs by using snapshots         | General-purpose, high-performance simulation      | Efficient simulation for Clifford circuits         |\n"
"| **Noise model**     | Automatically applies noise model from QPU snapshots | Custom or based on real QPU calibration data      | Ideal for noise-free simulations                   |\n"
"| **Circuit size**    | Limited to the capabilities of the mimicked QPU  | Can handle larger circuits               | Suitable for very large circuits (hundreds of qubits) |\n"
"| **Results**         | Moderate runtime for QPU-specific tests          | Shorter runtime for a wide range of simulations    | Extremely fast, suitable for stabilizer circuits  |\n"
"| **Use case**        | Testing transpiler and QPU-specific behavior     | General development, custom noise models          | Large stabilizer circuits, error correction        |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Simulator           | Fake Backends                                   | AerSimulator                                       | Clifford Simulation                                |\n"
"|---------------------|-------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|\n"
"| **Layunin**         | Ginagaya ang mga partikular na IBM&reg; QPU sa pamamagitan ng mga snapshot         | General-purpose, high-performance simulation      | Episyenteng simulation para sa mga Clifford circuit         |\n"
"| **Noise model**     | Awtomatikong inilalapat ang noise model mula sa mga QPU snapshot | Custom o batay sa tunay na QPU calibration data      | Perpekto para sa mga noise-free na simulation                   |\n"
"| **Laki ng Circuit**    | Limitado sa mga kakayahan ng ginagayang QPU  | Kayang hawakan ang mas malalaking circuit               | Angkop para sa napakalalaking circuit (daan-daang qubit) |\n"
"| **Mga Resulta**         | Katamtamang runtime para sa mga QPU-specific na test          | Mas maikling runtime para sa malawak na hanay ng mga simulation    | Napakabilis, angkop para sa mga stabilizer circuit  |\n"
"| **Use case**        | Pag-test ng Transpiler at QPU-specific na gawi     | Pangkalahatang development, custom na noise model          | Malalaking stabilizer circuit, error correction        |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"For most users, `AerSimulator` is a good choice, due to its flexibility and performance. However, if your work targets a specific QPU, a fake backend might be a better choice.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Para sa karamihan ng mga user, ang `AerSimulator` ay isang magandang pagpipilian, dahil sa flexibility at performance nito. Gayunpaman, kung ang iyong trabaho ay nakatutok sa isang partikular na QPU, maaaring mas magandang pagpipilian ang isang fake backend.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Fake backends {#fake-backends}"
msgstr "Fake backends {#fake-backends}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [fake backends](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/fake-provider) mimic the behaviors of IBM QPUs by using snapshots. "
"The snapshots contain important information about the QPU, such as the "
"coupling map, basis gates, and qubit properties, which are useful for "
"testing the transpiler and performing noisy simulations of the QPU.  The "
"noise model from the snapshot is automatically applied during simulation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ginagaya ng mga [fake backend](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/fake-provider) ang mga gawi ng IBM QPU sa pamamagitan ng mga "
"snapshot. Naglalaman ang mga snapshot ng mahahalagang impormasyon tungkol sa"
" QPU, tulad ng coupling map, basis gates, at mga katangian ng qubit, na "
"kapaki-pakinabang para sa pag-test ng Transpiler at pagsasagawa ng mga noisy"
" simulation ng QPU. Ang noise model mula sa snapshot ay awtomatikong "
"inilalapat sa panahon ng simulation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example:\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "AerSimulator {#aersimulator}"
msgstr "AerSimulator {#aersimulator}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can use local testing mode with simulators from [Qiskit "
"Aer](/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-aer), which provides higher-performance "
"simulation that can handle larger circuits and [custom noise "
"models](/guides/build-noise-models). It also supports Clifford simulation "
"mode, which can efficiently simulate Clifford circuits with a large number "
"of qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari kang gumamit ng local testing mode kasama ang mga simulator mula sa "
"[Qiskit Aer](/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-aer), na nagbibigay ng higher-"
"performance na simulation na kayang hawakan ang mas malalaking circuit at "
"[custom na noise model](/guides/build-noise-models). Sinusuportahan din nito"
" ang Clifford simulation mode, na kayang episyenteng i-simulate ang mga "
"Clifford circuit na may malaking bilang ng qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example with sessions, without noise:\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa na may sessions, walang noise:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"The following code block will return an error for users on the Open Plan, because it uses sessions. Workloads on the Open Plan can run only in [job mode](/guides/execution-modes#job-mode) or [batch mode](/guides/execution-modes#batch-mode).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Ang sumusunod na code block ay magbabalik ng error para sa mga user sa Open Plan, dahil gumagamit ito ng sessions. Ang mga workload sa Open Plan ay maaari lamang tumakbo sa [job mode](/guides/execution-modes#job-mode) o [batch mode](/guides/execution-modes#batch-mode).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To simulate with noise, specify a QPU (quantum hardware) and submit it to "
"Aer.  Aer builds a noise model based on the calibration data from that QPU "
"and instantiates an Aer backend with that model.  If you prefer, you can "
"[build a noise model](/guides/build-noise-models).\n"
msgstr ""
"Para mag-simulate na may noise, tumukoy ng QPU (quantum hardware) at isumite"
" ito sa Aer. Nagtatayo ang Aer ng noise model batay sa calibration data mula"
" sa QPU na iyon at nag-instantiate ng Aer backend na may modelong iyon. Kung"
" mas gusto mo, maaari kang [gumawa ng noise model](/guides/build-noise-"
"models).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example with noise:\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa na may noise:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"clifford-sim\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"clifford-sim\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Clifford simulation {#clifford-simulation}"
msgstr "Clifford simulation {#clifford-simulation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because Clifford circuits can be simulated efficiently with verifiable "
"results, Clifford simulation is a very useful tool. For an in-depth example,"
" see [Efficient simulation of stabilizer circuits with Qiskit Aer "
"primitives](/guides/simulate-stabilizer-circuits).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil episyenteng ma-si-simulate ang mga Clifford circuit at napapatunayan "
"ang mga resulta nito, ang Clifford simulation ay isang napaka-kapaki-"
"pakinabang na tool. Para sa isang malalim na halimbawa, tingnan ang "
"[Episyenteng simulation ng mga stabilizer circuit gamit ang Qiskit Aer "
"primitives](/guides/simulate-stabilizer-circuits).\n"
